 # Changelog
 
 All notable changes to the `harness-bootstrap` package. See `references/00-overview.md` for the full package description and versioning rules (patch/minor/major, same as `skill-authoring.md`'s "Bootstrap template versioning").
+
+## 7.4.0
+
+Fixes and improvements found while running a live `/dev` session against the
+deployed skill, all applied to `canonical/skills/dev` (and `design` where the
+same duration-formatting change applies). Design skill template 3.1.0 → 3.2.0,
+dev skill template 2.1.0 → 2.2.0.
+
+- **Trackerless local ID prefix bug**: `TEMPLATE.md` and
+  `references/01-context-gathering.md` generated `DESIGN-YYYYMMDD-XXXX` for
+  dev's own trackerless story IDs — copy-pasted verbatim from the design
+  skill's pattern. Corrected to `DEV-YYYYMMDD-XXXX`.
+- **Task-tracking contradiction**: `TEMPLATE.md`'s "Stage tasks" section said
+  to create the six stage tasks "before Phase 1," while Phase 1 said "DO NOT
+  call any tools... until the developer replies yes" — since `TaskCreate` is a
+  tool call, an agent following Phase 1 literally would never create tasks.
+  Clarified that task-tracking setup happens right after the Idempotency
+  check resolves, before the Phase 1 prompt, and is exempt from that gate —
+  stated on both sides of the contradiction so either entry point resolves it
+  the same way.
+- **Test stage Build check ignored ticket scope**: `references/05-test.md`
+  Step 3 unconditionally ran `{{NX_BUILD_CMD}}` (an app build) for every
+  ticket, contradicting Step 7's own "blindly running all NX checks on an
+  infra ticket wastes time" rule just below it. Now runs whichever check(s)
+  actually fit what the plan touched — Terraform validate for infra changes,
+  NX build for app code, both for a mixed-scope ticket, neither forced when
+  it doesn't apply.
+- **`@architect` audit trigger too broad**: "the plan touches infrastructure
+  stacks" forced a full HLD audit even for a routine like-for-like resource
+  addition (e.g. one more container in an already-reviewed Cosmos account).
+  Narrowed to actual topology/boundary changes — new resource type, new
+  network path/exposure, new service, a removal-policy or IAM change.
+- **Plan step granularity**: added a rule to `references/03-plan.md` — within
+  a single NX-project/concern step, split further along testable units when
+  more than one exists (data/schema, then core logic, then wiring), while a
+  genuinely atomic unit stays one step. A decomposition floor, not a mandate
+  to always split.
+- **New Stage Metrics table for dev**, mirroring design's per-stage view:
+  `dev-metrics.mjs`'s `report()` now renders a `## Stage Metrics` section
+  (all six lifecycle stages) in addition to the existing per-implementation-step
+  `## Step Metrics` table, each with its own marker pair
+  (`dev-metrics-stage:*` / `dev-metrics-step:*`, replacing the single
+  `dev-metrics:*`). `constants.mjs`, `templates/report.md`, and the test
+  suite's marker assertions updated to match.
+- **Explanatory Elapsed/Work/Wait columns + human-readable durations** (both
+  design and dev): added a `humanDuration()` helper to both `utils.mjs`
+  copies, formatting durations as `1h 2m 4s` / `2m 4s` / `4s` instead of raw
+  fractional seconds, used throughout both metrics CLIs' generated reports;
+  added a plain-language definition of what Elapsed/Work/Wait each measure
+  (and why they need not sum exactly) to both report templates and the
+  generated report text.
 
